    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form so owners can supply `addressLine1` (+ optional `addressLine2`), `city`, and `postcode`, while the flat `address` remains accepted for backward compatibility.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so they appear on both the request DTO and the response DTO), and removed `address` from the `required` list. `city` and `telephone` stay required, so a missing city still yields a 400 from bean validation.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` persistent columns with getters/setters (MapStruct auto-maps them by name).\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Replaced the single flat-address normalization with a new `applyAddress` helper that:\n   - Rejects the create (400 `InvalidAddressException`) only when neither a non-blank `addressLine1` nor a non-blank flat `address` is present.\n   - When the structured form is present, normalizes each supplied line (upper-case, whitespace collapse, `ST`\u2192`STREET` etc.), stores `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, and sets the composed `address` = normalized `addressLine1` + a single space + normalized `addressLine2` (the second part only when `addressLine2` is present).\n   - Falls back to the normalized flat `address` otherwise.\n\n   Because everything downstream (household hash, postcode validation, locality) reads the stored `owner.getAddress()` / `city` / `postcode`, it now uses the structured value when present and the flat value otherwise.\n\nThe relevant checkpoint tests (Cp01 required-fields, Cp12 normalization, Cp44 structured + composed `address` + flat backward-compat) all pass, as does the full suite.",
